        "content": "<p>jrandolf opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14842\">PR #14842</a> from <code>jrandolf:wast-record-field-count</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The record case in the wast harness compared <code>e.len() != e.len()</code>, which is always false, so an <code>assert_return</code> with fewer (or more) record fields than the actual value passed as long as the fields that were zipped together matched. This compares against the actual record and includes both counts in the error, and adds a test of the harness itself.</p>\n<p>I came across this while looking at map support, but it's not map specific.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
